prompt:
Turn this clean 3D frame of a real apartment into a photorealistic interior photograph.

Keep the scene exactly as given — this is a render of a real flat under design, not a new picture:
- same camera, same focal length, same horizon; do not re-frame, do not zoom, do not straighten walls;
- same room geometry: walls, openings, window and door positions, ceiling height 2.7 m;
- same furniture: every object stays in its place, with its size, orientation and shape; add nothing, remove nothing;
- same window views and the same time of day as the light in the frame suggests;
- no people, no pets, no text, no watermark.

Style and tone (правь этот раздел под себя — он уходит в промпт как есть):
- calm modern interior, muted natural palette: warm greys, sand, oak, off-white walls;
- matte finishes, soft contrast, no glossy plastic look, no HDR halos;
- daylight from the windows plus the lamps already visible in the frame; soft shadows, no hard studio light;
- materials read honestly: oak veneer, painted MDF fronts, linen textiles, matte porcelain tile, brushed metal;
- photographic look: full-frame camera, no fisheye, natural depth of field, slight film grain.

